@startuml
!include a5-style.iuml
hide empty members
top to bottom direction
title Figure A5-2: Class Diagram - Services, Billing, Calendar, Chat, Case File and Reminders (updated)

class BillingService {
  + statementForCase(caseId) : CaseStatement
  + allEntries() : List<BillingEntry>
  + generateInvoicePdf(case, st, settled) : byte[]
  - extractAiClaimAmount(caseId) : double
}
class FirmBillingOverview {
  + matters : List<FirmMatterBillingRow>
  + firmBilledInclVat : double
  + outstandingDebtors : double
  + trustHeld : double
}
class TrustAccountingService {
  + statementForCase(caseId) : TrustStatement
  + transfersToBusinessForCase(caseId) : double
  + recordTransaction(caseId, type, amount) : void
}
class ExcelWorkbookService {
  + build(cases, docs, billing, trust) : byte[]
}
class UserService {
  + create(id, name, email, password, role) : void
  + verify(email, password) : User
  + setActive(id, active) : void
}
class CaseService {
  + assignClient(caseId, clientId) : void
}
class CalendarSyncService {
  + syncOne(deadline) : String
  + unsyncOne(deadline) : String
  + testConnection() : String
}
interface CalendarGateway {
  + createEvent(deadline, case) : Receipt
  + deleteEvent(eventId, calendarId) : void
  + probe() : String
}
class LocalCalendarGateway {
  + writes calendar.ics
}
class GoogleCalendarGateway {
  - cached access token
  + retries 429 and 5xx
}
class AuditService {
  + record(user, action, details)
  + verifyChain() : boolean
}

BillingService ..> FirmBillingOverview : builds
BillingService --> TrustAccountingService : settles from trust
BillingService --> AuditService
TrustAccountingService --> AuditService : overdraft check
ExcelWorkbookService --> BillingService
ExcelWorkbookService --> TrustAccountingService
UserService --> AuditService
CaseService --> UserService : links client
CalendarSyncService --> CalendarGateway
CalendarGateway <|.. LocalCalendarGateway
CalendarGateway <|.. GoogleCalendarGateway
CalendarSyncService --> AuditService
class ChatController {
  + ask(ctx) : POST /api/chat
}
class ChatbotService {
  + {static} classify(text) : Intent
  + answer(session, text) : Reply
  - resolveCase(text, visible) : Case
}
class CaseFileService {
  + render(case, summary, deadlines, st, trust, at) : byte[]
}
class ReminderService {
  + runOnce() : RunResult
  + recent(limit) : List<Reminder>
  - recipientsFor(case) : List<String>
}
class Reminder {
  id, deadlineId, recipient
  subject, body, status
  QUEUED | SENT | FAILED
}
class MailSender {
  + isConfigured() : boolean
  + send(to, subject, body) : void
}

ChatController --> ChatbotService
ChatbotService --> CaseService : reads cases
ChatbotService --> DeadlineService : next date
ChatbotService --> BillingService : amount owed
ChatbotService --> TrustAccountingService : trust credit
ChatbotService --> MessageService : unread count
CaseFileService ..> BillingService : fee note figures
CaseFileService ..> TrustAccountingService : trust figures
ReminderService --> DeadlineService : due deadlines
ReminderService --> CaseService : recipients on case
ReminderService --> UserService : client email
ReminderService --> MailSender : sends when configured
ReminderService --> AuditService
ReminderService ..> Reminder : creates
note right of TrustAccountingService
  Section 86 trust rule: a settlement is
  rejected when the amount exceeds the
  available trust balance.
end note
@enduml
